From 64d21a839e2acfa465b7d31422ffaa3b04ca4841 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:37:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/70] ppc32: 32-bit instruction selector for the
 Turboshaft-only backend

13.6's instruction-selector-ppc.cc is no longer the template<Adapter>
file the 12.4 series patched: the Turbofan adapter is gone, the file is
Turboshaft-only (4016 -> 2912 lines) and every one of the 31
V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 blocks the 12.4 tree carried went with it, so the
12.4 patches that complete the 32-bit selector (0005 "complete the 32-bit
guards in instruction selector and code generator", 0006 "restore the
pair-op visitors", 0041 "guard the turboshaft Word64-compare sites", 0050
"table switch without the 64-bit index zero-extension" and the selector
hunk of 0014 "do not advertise round/popcnt machine ops") have nothing
left to apply to.  This commit re-derives all of that against the 13.6
file (reference: the pristine-12.4 blocks, `git diff cmake-12.4~7
ppc-darwin-12.4` on this file, and ia32's 13.6 pair-op visitors for the
Turboshaft spelling):

- 59 Word64/Int64/Uint64 visitors and their helpers (VisitTryTruncateDouble,
  IsContiguousMask64, VisitWord64Compare, the four Word64Atomic* visitors,
  the VISIT_ATOMIC_BINOP64 half of the atomic binop macro, the I64x2
  splat/lane visitors) sit under V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64: on a 32-bit target
  the generic selector defines every one of them (instruction-selector.cc,
  V8_TARGET_ARCH_32_BIT and the 64-bit-atomics block), and node/gnmirror-
  style cross-check: all 64 names of those generic lists are now guarded.
- the Int32Pair{Add,Sub,Mul} and Word32Pair{Shl,Shr,Sar} visitors (the
  generic selector marks them unsupported only under V8_TARGET_ARCH_64_BIT,
  so a 32-bit backend must define them) in Turboshaft form: OptionalOpIndex
  projections, CanBeImmediate(kShift64Imm) for the shift count.  The pair
  opcodes they select are still in instruction-codes-ppc.h and the
  scheduler, and the previous commit restored their code generation.
- VisitBitcastWord32PairToFloat64 selects kPPC_DoubleConstruct on 32-bit
  (13.6's kPPC_DoubleFromWord32Pair assembles both words in one 64-bit GPR;
  its code-generator case is now 64-bit-only as well).
- SelectLoadOpcode (both overloads) and VisitStoreCommon: uncompressed
  tagged values are pointer-sized (LoadWordU32 / StoreWord32), Int64 /
  Uint64 / kWord64 are unreachable, the write-barrier path's extra
  4-byte-alignment test is 64-bit-only (stw has no DS-form constraint).
- VisitWordCompareZero's Word64 comparison and Word64Sub/BitwiseAnd
  fusions, VisitSwitch's Uint32ToUint64 index extension and the
  round/popcnt entries of SupportedMachineOperatorFlags are 64-bit-only,
  exactly as the 12.4 series left them.

Not carried here: the Float32Sqrt/Float64Sqrt routing to libm (depends on
the kIeee754Float64Sqrt opcode that 0030 adds; done when 0030 is rebased).

Rebased onto 14.6 (node 26): instruction-selector-ppc.cc is de-templated
there (InstructionSelectorT<Adapter> -> InstructionSelector, operands read
through `op.input(i)` instead of `input_at(node, i)`, which no longer
exists), so the patch was re-derived mechanically (template names renamed,
`template <typename Adapter>` lines dropped) and five hunks by hand:
SelectLoadOpcode's uncompressed-tagged cases (14.6 added USE(result_rep)
and the AnyTagged case), the Word64 Clz/Popcnt/Ctz/ReverseBits and
Word64AtomicLoad guards (new `op.input(0)` bodies), and the atomic binop
macro, whose Word64 half is dropped in favour of the PPC64-only
VISIT_ATOMIC_BINOP64 copy.  The pair-op visitors now read their operands
through Word32PairBinopOp::{left,right}_{low,high}() as ia32/arm do at
14.6 (the pair shifts are Word32PairBinopOps whose right_low() is the
shift count).  node/linkaudit.py on the result: the one benign duplicate
(the VisitStackPointerGreaterThan overload pair) and no missing visitor
beyond the 13.6 set.
